# NOTE: pyarrow/pandas were removed — they were unused anywhere in the codebase and the
# pinned pyarrow (<15) has no wheels for newer Python (3.13+), forcing a source build that
# fails on Windows. Re-add (and a real consumer) if Parquet/dataframe support is needed.
#
# CROSS-PLATFORM LOCK NOTE: requirements.txt is hashed and includes pywin32 (a Windows-only
# transitive of mcp, via semantic-kernel) under a `sys_platform == "win32"` marker so
# `pip install --require-hashes` works on Windows too. Linux pip-compile evaluates that
# marker away, so if you regenerate requirements.txt, either re-add the pywin32 block or
# regenerate with `uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes requirements.in`.

